8:  {name:'June Holloway',role:'The old compass',glyph:'☽',need:'SHADOW · MEANING',story:'June has just retired. Without the title on her door, she feels like a house with its sign taken down. She asks if a life can have a second beginning without pretending the first did not happen.',tags:['The Wanderer','A threshold'],choices:[{title:'Map what remains',copy:'Name the values that outlive a role.',cost:0,currency:'ink',effects:{shadow:4,anima:4,trust:4,insight:1},result:'June finds that care, not achievement, was the thread all along.'},{title:'Sit at the threshold',copy:'Let the in-between be a place, not a problem.',cost:1,currency:'ink',effects:{shadow:5,child:3,trust:4},result:'June leaves the door ajar. She does not need to name the next room yet.'}]},
